A||||8||GTMike||how much horse power do you lose for high elevation||||1||
Z||000000||GTMike||07-12-2001||07:47 PM||||well i just got my car.  i flew out las vages and got the car.  las vages is around 2000 feet above sea leve.  the car has so much power. i could fish tail and spin the hell out of the tirs. (ihad to test her out)<P>so i got home to colorado where i'm at 5500 feet above sea level and it seems i have lost some power.   i just wanted to know how much horse power is lost when going to higher elevation.  <P>i plan on useing some bolt on parts to achieve the same horse power that i had down in las vages.   such as cold air intake.  msd ignition. and possibably and under drive pully.  <P>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Wolfhound||07-12-2001||08:03 PM||||Guess mine runs good because of 300 Ft. Elevation. Pistons pack more, thicker air.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>When I was 10 years old on the 4th of July In 1956, I ran around and threw snowball at my sister on top of pikes peak at the "Hill Climb" I became unconsious and had to be carried down on the Cog Train. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||07-12-2001||08:07 PM||||One answer: LOTS. Less air, les combustion. You can feel the difference driving up the mountains.||||reg||6
Z||000003||wkayl||07-12-2001||08:34 PM||||I plan on driving up Pikes Peak sometime this summer.  I'll post pictures when I do.||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||07-12-2001||09:05 PM||||About 15-20% less power. Add  about 1.17 seconds to your 0-60 time and .8 seconds to your quarter mile time.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||GTMike||07-12-2001||09:08 PM||||hummm any suggestions on getting some of those hps back?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mach10||07-12-2001||09:10 PM||||Nitrous, turbo. Replace the air you lost. don't worry though, the slow-down is across the board. I.E., everyone experiences about the same loss.||||reg||13
Z||000007||88formula||07-12-2001||09:29 PM||||What he said above. Turbochargers and Superchargers are a way to get beck that lost oxygen. I would go with a Design One Turbocharger. <A HREF="http://www.design1systems.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.design1systems.com</A>  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||GTMike||07-13-2001||01:58 PM||||those are good ideas.  i was thinking for that amount of money i would just save up a little more cash and go with the 3800 sc.  my engine only has 44k on it.  so i just wanted to try to get 15-20 more horses  for the time being.  i probably wont do and eng. swap for a few years.   <P>||||reg||1
